    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0188" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p1/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/4–352: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United Nations Command
                            (Ridgway) to the
                            Department of the Army</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>operational immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-04-16T17:46:00+09:00">April 16, 1952—5:46
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>CX 67005. 1. At the completion of Opn <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Scatter</hi> it will be nec to
                    reclassify those South Korean, North Korean, and Chinese POWs refusing to return to enemy control. Our
                    present planned procedure is to reclassify and segregate: <list>
                        <label><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>.</label>
                        <item>South Korean POWs refusing return to
                            enemy control as “civilian internees.”</item>
                        <pb facs="0189" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/>
                        <label><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>.</label>
                        <item>North Korean and Chinese POWs
                            refusing return to enemy control as “displaced persons in protective
                            custody of the United Nations Command.”</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>2. CGArEight would be instructed to treat
                    “displaced persons in protective custody of United Nations Command” in
                    accordance with the humanitarian principles of the 1949 Geneva Prisoner of War
                    Conventions. The administration of civilian internees would continue to be in
                    accordance with our C 58702, Dec. 51.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d91-f1"/></p>
                <p>3. Rosters of individuals reclassified in accordance with procedure outlined in
                    Para 1 would be furnd ICRC.</p>
                <p>4. Rqst approval of planned procedure outlined above.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
